  "download_disabled": false,
  "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\">The dataset contains raw and cropped images for industrial smoke segmentation. The task is to identify the pixels in the image that belongs to a part of the industrial smoke emission. The standard way for using this dataset is to cast the task as pixel-level classification. However, one can also go for the polygon-based image segmentation approach. We have in total 900 raw images with 1209 polygons. Among them, 7 raw images have no smoke. Also, we have in total 2074 cropped images, and among them, 1109 images have smoke (and have pixel-level masks).</p><p dir=\"ltr\">If you use the dataset, please cite this technical report (that describes details about the dataset):</p><ul><li>Yen-Chia Hsu, Despoina Touska. 2026. IJmond Industrial Smoke Segmentation Dataset. arXiv preprint arXiv:2603.23754. <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.23754\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.23754</a></li></ul><p><br></p>",
